    "create_time": 1781489137.551,
    "update_time": null,
    "content": {
     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "Draft (112 words):\n\n> **R2, label reliability.** We thank R2 for raising this. κ = 0.71 (Light's κ; Krippendorff's α = 0.71) was computed on the three raters' *independent* labels for 412 windows, **before** any discussion or adjudication. Disagreements were then resolved by discussion, and the resolved labels, not the agreement statistic, were used for training. We will (1) state the order of computation explicitly in Sec. 4.2, (2) add per-state one-vs-rest κ, which shows disagreement concentrated in *stalled-after-error* vs. *productive*, and (3) include the labeling guide (v3) with decision rules for that boundary as supplementary material.\n\nIt concedes the underspecification without conceding inflation, and every promise is cheap to keep."
     ]
    },
    "status": "finished_successfully",
