  "390059e7-3fae-40ea-8915-22b247a50ba3": {
   "id": "390059e7-3fae-40ea-8915-22b247a50ba3",
   "message": {
    "id": "390059e7-3fae-40ea-8915-22b247a50ba3",
    "author": {
     "role": "assistant",
     "name": null,
     "metadata": {}
    },
    "create_time": 1781489311.062,
    "update_time": null,
    "content": {
     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "Promise something you can definitely run before camera-ready, scoped to data you already have or can get. Example:\n\n> **R1, generalization.** We agree this is the main limitation. Our deployment covers one course (CS2, two lab sections). For the camera-ready we will add a cross-course analysis applying the classifier, without retraining, to [N] sessions from [second course/semester], reporting per-state F1, and we will expand the Limitations section to discuss course-specific features (e.g., assignment-specific error types).\n\nFill the brackets only if Yan has confirmed access to that data. If not, the safer version is:\n\n> …we will add a cross-course analysis on sessions from an additional course offering where available, and in any case expand the Limitations section…\n\nThe second version is weaker but impossible to break."
     ]
    },
